## js/src/parse.js

This file contines the parse function. The
parse function is a core utility function
that takes the raw bubblescript as a textual
representation and produces a pare tree
which can be subsequently analyized or
evaluated. This function is overloaded in
order to provide a clean seperation of
concerns. Before a stream of characters or
string can be parse with this function, it
must be tokenized, other wise known a
lexically analyzied. Lexacal analsys is
performed by the tokenize function. When the
parse function recieves a string, it first
tokenizes the string by calling tokenize,
then parses and retirns the result. The
parse function may also be called directly
with the result of calling tokenize.

The parse function is also akata. This is a
translation of the word parse, but in the
standard english version of Bubblescript,
the proper name of this function is parse.
